{
  "data": {
    "id": 1161246,
    "name": "Seckel Pears",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The </span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seckel_pear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Seckel pear</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> is a tiny, exceptionally sweet heirloom fruit often called the \"sugar pear\" or \"candy pear\".</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Flavor &amp; Texture:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> Rich, spicy, and honeyed sweetness with firm, juicy, and smooth flesh.</span></p><ul class=\"lexical-text-editor--list-ul\"><li value=\"1\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Perfect for kids and lunchboxes because of its bite-sized shape.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Canning:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> Small enough to be canned or pickled whole.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Cooking:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> Excellent for poaching, roasting, and pairing with cheese boards or desserts. </span></li></ul>",
